{
  "topic": "challenger",
  "ttsScript": "Seven people died on the Space Shuttle Challenger. NASA knew it would happen. The night before, engineers begged them not to launch. NASA called it a malfunction. Unforeseeable. Unpredictable. But engineers had warned them for months. The rubber O-rings cracked in cold weather. Launch morning, it was 36 degrees. Engineers told NASA the O-rings would fail. NASA asked them to reconsider. Their managers overruled them. Millions of children watched live from their classrooms. Seventy-three seconds after launch, the O-ring failed. Richard Feynman proved it at the hearing. He dropped an O-ring in a glass of ice water. It cracked. A six cent rubber ring. That is what they ignored.",
